'' A derived value into a type built from its BASE -- 'constructor( byref as const Shape )'
'' given a Circle, 'constructor( byref as const Plain )' a PlainKid -- through a byref
'' const, a byref and a byval parameter. fbc-modern runs the constructor every time (lines
'' measured); tiko judged the byref forms as pointees, Holder against Circle, and refused
'' them (TKO0698). See UdtArgBuilds_ in symbols/assigncheck.tiko.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/udt-derived-ctor-arg.bas -o tests/codegen/udtderivedctorarg.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/udtderivedctorarg.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/udtderivedctorarg.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C shape:circle r=5 spec=x
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C plain:8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R shape:circle r=5 spec=x
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: R plain:8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: V shape:circle r=5 spec=x
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: V plain:8
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: C kind 1
